Defend treatment-to-consumer service and its limits (@wu-distribution-review: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #water-and-sanitation "../collection/From-a-drain-to-a-receiving-environment.lingua#r_63NHMW0Q4G8VY4ENPKEEQQGWQN") { r_30VN17MXVWHYGX6RTV84CYYA83
**Read:** Complete the selected membrane, UV, corrosion and network studies, with [WHO distribution-system reference](../sources/Water-Safety-in-Distribution-WHO.lingua#r_4Z856ZAJVQZR5T72ZP9ZZ92YZF) and [water safety plan manual](../sources/Water-Safety-Plan-Manual-WHO.lingua#r_3JMZKS3FG80FKX9YRQPEJMA4VD) for the system-wide argument. Keep the substantial source readings and original calculations together rather than replacing them with a list of technologies.

Present a source-to-consumer case whose treatment, hydraulic and quality accounts agree. Explain the path to a novice, defend each model and its evidence, and preserve uncertainty at the interfaces. Include gross/net water, residuals, power, chemicals, sensors, material history, maintenance, staff and interruption response.

Test an unfamiliar combined event: source deterioration during a power interruption, an unavailable unit during peak demand, or a treatment change affecting distribution materials. Show where your evidence remains applicable and where it does not. Compare two ways of improving service, including their dependencies on transport, suppliers, laboratories and skilled work.

For scholarly depth, reproduce an identified study, compare a competing explanation and develop an independently checked extension. State what was actually performed, what used published data and what remains proposed. Defend the limits of every safety or performance claim.

**Current boundary:** This completes a demanding reading-and-investigation section, not the entire water trail or professional authorization. Continue through collection, wastewater biology, residuals and recovery; industrial service/reuse, whole-system control and research follow later. Those subjects retain their own full depth; they are not implied by a successful drinking-water case.

**Continue:** [From a drain to a receiving environment](../collection/From-a-drain-to-a-receiving-environment.lingua#r_63NHMW0Q4G8VY4ENPKEEQQGWQN).
